{"papers":[{"id":"openalex:W7225049229","title":"End-To-End Petrophysical Operations with Agentic AI: A Horizontal Carbonate Reservoir Well Case Study from a Mature Onshore Field, Abu Dhabi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2118/235583-ms","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://doi.org/10.2118/235583-ms"],"alternate_titles":["End-To-End Petrophysical Operations with Agentic AI: A Horizontal Carbonate Reservoir Well Case Study from a Mature Onshore Field, Abu Dhabi"],"published":"2026-11-02","authors":["M. Ahmad Nazlan","Zoheir Chikhi","M. Y. Al Blooshi","T. Alhosani","M. Al-Hammadi","M. Sulaiman"],"abstract":"Abstract Petrophysical work follows a well from planning through drilling and into completion, and at each step it usually passes between different specialists, vendor software, and email threads. This paper describes an in-house agentic artificial-intelligence assistant that brings those steps together behind one interface driven by text and voice. The system was validated end to end on a horizontal development well, denoted Well A here for confidentiality, drilled through a heterogeneous carbonate reservoir in a mature onshore field in Abu Dhabi. The assistant runs a fleet of nine configuration-driven skills grouped into two co-equal suites. A planning suite covers a well-data registry, document compilation, logging-program generation, cement-bond evaluation, and a logging-activity dashboard. An operations suite covers a vendor-aware quick-look interpretation pipeline, a production-log...","companies":["Microsoft"],"matched_orgs":["Microsoft"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["openalex"],"source":"openalex","work_type":"conference-paper","doi":"https://doi.org/10.2118/235583-ms","openalex_id":"https://openalex.org/W7225049229","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":37,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Abu Dhabi National Oil (United Arab Emirates)","Microsoft (United States)"],"concepts":[{"id":"https://openalex.org/C46293882","display_name":"Petrophysics","score":0.7182999849319458},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C127313418","display_name":"Geology","score":0.6996999979019165},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C79581498","display_name":"Suite","score":0.4925999939441681},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C2780659211","display_name":"Carbonate","score":0.4657000005245209},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C25197100","display_name":"Drilling","score":0.435699999332428},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C2781219549","display_name":"Infill","score":0.4309000074863434},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C122792734","display_name":"Lithology","score":0.32839998602867126},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C548895740","display_name":"Petroleum","score":0.3208000063896179}],"official_report":false,"quality_signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0},"evidence":[{"source":"openalex","url":"https://doi.org/10.2118/235583-ms","labs":["Microsoft"],"signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"abstract_and_subject_metadata","ai_research_source":"","matched_terms":["language model","agentic","AI"],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"conference-paper"},"ai_research_source":""},{"id":"openalex:W7225046620","title":"A Framework for Efficient Well Control Modeling in Machine Learning Surrogates","url":"https://doi.org/10.2118/236261-ms","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://doi.org/10.2118/236261-ms"],"alternate_titles":["A Framework for Efficient Well Control Modeling in Machine Learning Surrogates"],"published":"2026-11-02","authors":["W. Diab","T. Onishi","M. Corrales","Mohammed Al Kobaisi"],"abstract":"Abstract Numerical reservoir simulators are computationally prohibitive for many-query tasks such as field development planning; which motivates a new generation of machine learning surrogates that promise significant speed ups over traditional solvers. A persistent challenge in that work is the treatment of dynamic well controls and sparse, time-dependent well data. Surrogates that reproduce cell-centered fields accurately often leave the quantities an engineer actually depend on, namely bottomhole pressure, phase rates, water cut, and gas-oil ratio, either outside the model or regressed by unconstrained output heads that need not respect rate control or the underlying inflow physics. We address this by coupling a three-dimensional Temporal Neural Operator (TNO), whose branch and trunk factorization decouples spatial geological heterogeneity from temporal well control inputs, to an anal...","companies":["NVIDIA"],"matched_orgs":["NVIDIA"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["openalex"],"source":"openalex","work_type":"conference-paper","doi":"https://doi.org/10.2118/236261-ms","openalex_id":"https://openalex.org/W7225046620","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":37,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Khalifa University of Science and Technology","Nvidia (United States)"],"concepts":[{"id":"https://openalex.org/C41008148","display_name":"Computer science","score":0.5483999848365784},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C154945302","display_name":"Artificial intelligence","score":0.5177000164985657},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C50644808","display_name":"Artificial neural network","score":0.5080000162124634},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C2778904306","display_name":"Well control","score":0.46799999475479126},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C2779538338","display_name":"Completion (oil and gas wells)","score":0.454800009727478},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C2776132308","display_name":"Inflow","score":0.45239999890327454},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C185798385","display_name":"Benchmark (surveying)","score":0.44110000133514404},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C17020691","display_name":"Operator (biology)","score":0.42320001125335693}],"official_report":false,"quality_signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0},"evidence":[{"source":"openalex","url":"https://doi.org/10.2118/236261-ms","labs":["NVIDIA"],"signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"abstract_and_subject_metadata","ai_research_source":"","matched_terms":["machine learning","neural network","artificial intelligence","neural operator","neural"],"concept_ids":["https://openalex.org/C154945302","https://openalex.org/C119857082"],"work_type":"conference-paper"},"ai_research_source":""},{"id":"openalex:W7225038798","title":"Single-cell perturbation prediction near experimental reproducibility with GENESIS","url":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.10.30.763081","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.10.30.763081"],"alternate_titles":["Single-cell perturbation prediction near experimental reproducibility with GENESIS"],"published":"2026-11-01","authors":["Riccardo Conci","Davide D’Ascenzo","Sebastiano Cultrera di Montesano","Srivatsan Raghavan","Peter S. Winter","Eliezer M. Van Allen","Lorin A. Crawford","William E. Lotter"],"abstract":"Single-cell perturbation atlases now measure cellular responses across millions of cells, but the number of possible combinations of biological contexts, perturbations, doses and other experimental variables make exhaustive measurements infeasible. Here, we present GENESIS (Generative ENErgy-based Single-cell Intervention Simulator), a generative framework that predicts single-cell response distributions directly from the covariates defining an experimental condition. GENESIS uses a lightweight neural network trained with the energy score, a strictly proper scoring rule for distributions. We introduce an experiment-calibrated evaluation framework in which prediction error is interpreted relative to the reproducibility of repeated measurements of the same condition. Across the Tahoe-100M small-molecule atlas and a large PBMC cytokine atlas, GENESIS significantly outperforms existing gener...","companies":["Microsoft"],"matched_orgs":["Microsoft"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["openalex"],"source":"openalex","work_type":"preprint","doi":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.10.30.763081","openalex_id":"https://openalex.org/W7225038798","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":37,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Broad Institute","Dana-Farber Cancer Institute","Harvard University","Microsoft Research (United Kingdom)"],"concepts":[{"id":"https://openalex.org/C9893847","display_name":"Reproducibility","score":0.6337000131607056},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C177918212","display_name":"Perturbation (astronomy)","score":0.5184000134468079},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C41008148","display_name":"Computer science","score":0.4569999873638153},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C39890363","display_name":"Generative grammar","score":0.43140000104904175},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C119043178","display_name":"Covariate","score":0.42899999022483826},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C167966045","display_name":"Generative model","score":0.3747999966144562},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C19619285","display_name":"Observational error","score":0.3700999915599823},{"id":"https://openalex.org/C154945302","display_name":"Artificial intelligence","score":0.3652999997138977}],"official_report":false,"quality_signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0},"evidence":[{"source":"openalex","url":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.10.30.763081","labs":["Microsoft"],"signals":{"affiliation_source":"OpenAlex","company_match_source":"OpenAlex authorship institution metadata","cited_by_count":0}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"abstract_and_subj